[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/30352948","html_url":"https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/issues/2470#issuecomment-30352948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/2470","id":30352948,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMzUyOTQ4","user":{"login":"davidsteinsland","id":125661,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTY2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125661?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland","html_url":"https://github.com/davidsteinsland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-12-11T19:17:42Z","updated_at":"2013-12-11T20:10:59Z","body":"It's because the way `Hash::extract()` works. Basically `Hash::combine()` is doing a:\n\n``` php\n$vals = Hash::extract($src, '{n}.second.title');\n```\n\nThis call does not return `null` if the value is not found; it simply return the one that does. When there's an inequality in the number of keys and values, one does not know which key hasn't got their value (or vice versa).\n\nI can see a fix for your issue, but what if it is a value which doesnt have a corresponding key? (Switch the two last arguments for your `combine()` call). What then?\n\nThis is what we would call \"undefined behavior\" in C, but I cannot see a fix which involves fixing both circumstances (without changing too much in the outlined methods).\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/30352948/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"davidsteinsland","id":125661,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTY2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125661?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland","html_url":"https://github.com/davidsteinsland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/30382747","html_url":"https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/issues/2470#issuecomment-30382747","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/2470","id":30382747,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMzgyNzQ3","user":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory","html_url":"https://github.com/markstory","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-12-12T01:45:00Z","updated_at":"2013-12-12T01:45:00Z","body":"One option that will possibly would solve this but may break other uses would be to throw exceptions when the length of both arrays is not equal. I will check how the native array_combine as it would be nice to reflect that behaviour if possible.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/30382747/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory","html_url":"https://github.com/markstory","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/30412158","html_url":"https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/issues/2470#issuecomment-30412158","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/2470","id":30412158,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNDEyMTU4","user":{"login":"nojimage","id":100564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU2NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage","html_url":"https://github.com/nojimage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-12-12T11:50:10Z","updated_at":"2013-12-12T11:50:10Z","body":"Thanks comments.\n\nIf `Hash::combine` returns correct pair, should be add another extract method that return a null value if it is key which doesn't have a corresponding value. It's complicated.\n\nThe array_combine throws E_WARNING if the number of elements in keys and values does not match.\nhttp://php.net/manual/en/function.array-combine.php\n\n`Hash::combine` throw an exception or warning, like array_combine.\nI think that this is better.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/30412158/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"nojimage","id":100564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU2NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage","html_url":"https://github.com/nojimage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nojimage/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/30415619","html_url":"https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/issues/2470#issuecomment-30415619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/2470","id":30415619,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNDE1NjE5","user":{"login":"davidsteinsland","id":125661,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTY2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125661?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland","html_url":"https://github.com/davidsteinsland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-12-12T12:20:02Z","updated_at":"2013-12-12T12:20:02Z","body":"1. `extract` should have that optional parameter, as its only use case would be here\n2. something tells me that your should probably normalize your array instead\n3. If anything, the `combine()` would throw an exception, but this looks kinda bad when Cake doesn't use exceptions for anything unless is a fatal error. I'm still pro-exceptions, but not perhaps in this regard.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/30415619/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"davidsteinsland","id":125661,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTY2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125661?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland","html_url":"https://github.com/davidsteinsland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidsteinsland/orgs","repos_url":"ht